senses.gloss:
(1) [TINOSPORA CORDIFOLIA (WILLD.) MIERS] (Bpn, p. 269-270;
Chopra) = T. CORDIFOLIA MIERS (Avk; Dgm, p. 25; Dgv, nr. 14; Dutt;
DWH 1, p. 54-56; Gul; HB; HK; Kav; KB 1, p. 77-80; Na 1, nr. 12;
Nadk. 1, nr. 2472; PA 1, 7, p. 13-27; Sanyal; V 3, p. 86; Vśs) =
MENISPERMUM CORDIFOLIUM WILLD. (Dutt; HK; Kav; KB 1, p. 77-
80; Nadk. 1, nr. 2472; PA 1, 7, p. 13-27; Vśs) [= M. CORDIFOLIUM
RUSSELL] (Ainslie 2, p. 377-378) = M. GLABRUM BURM. F. (PA 1, 7,
p. 13-27) = COCCULUS CORDIFOLIUS DC. (HK; MW; Nadk. 1, nr.
2472; PA 1, 7, p. 13-27; PW);
(2) TINOSPORA CRISPA MIERS (DWH 1, p. 64: known by the same
vernacular names as T. CORDIFOLIA; PA 1, 7, p. 32, footnote: used
sometimes as a substitute) = MENISPERMUM CRISPUM LINN.;
(3) T. MALABARICA MIERS (PA 1, 7, p. 32, footnote: used sometimes
as a substitute) = MENISPERMUM MALABARICUM LAM.;
(4) T. TOMENTOSA MIERS (PA 1, 7, p. 32, footnote: used sometimes
[]
as a substitute; PA considers 3) and 4) as synonyms) = MENISPERMUM
TOMENTOSUM ROXB.
